a00c2a84ff416b","cmd-dfe28cc25a1e4c23","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied with direct final behavior and successful persistence testing. The provider-wide restart protocol was completed coherently on both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered chronyd service, and restored time synchronization were captured, with lifecycle boot identities independently matching the executor evidence.","limitations":["Native package-health checks timed out in both lifecycle phases on both nodes, so package-manager consistency could not be assessed.","The lifecycle collector did not inventory `/etc/chrony.conf` or possible backup files; configuration state is therefore supported by executor commands rather than an independent final filesystem snapshot."]}
